  "caveats": {
    "caveat_1_single_fold_vs_ensemble": "This study evaluates single-fold out-of-fold predictions. The official HC18 challenge test submission used a 5-fold ensemble average of predicted ellipse parameters. Averaging across 5 independent fold models already reduces prediction variance and naturally shifts predictions toward the ensemble centroid.",
    "caveat_2_signed_difference_convention": "Both signed difference conventions are explicitly reported: (1) Under (y_true - y_pred), raw predictions have a mean signed bias of +1.2576 mm (median +1.3490 mm), confirming that the single-fold models systematically underestimated ground-truth HC. (2) Under (y_pred - y_true), raw signed mean is -1.2576 mm (median -1.3490 mm).",
    "caveat_3_no_challenge_submission_changes": "Zero changes are made to the official challenge submission CSVs (submission_ensemble_5fold.csv and submission_single_fold1.csv) or submission generation scripts. This audit is strictly observational on the existing held-out cross-validation records."
